:name: nucleus-m10-embedded
:description: Inject input.bin, load a GENERATED embedded-pattern firmware, run bounded, capture USART1.

# The Renode runtime script for the embedded-pattern backend's M10 bin
# (TASK-0048.01 emission + TASK-0048.02 value-correctness, generalised to
# examples 1/5/9 in TASK-0048.03). Unlike tests/renode/uart-smoke/run.resc
# (a hand-written sentinel firmware), the ELF this loads is GENERATED by
# `nucleus build --backend embedded-pattern --shim stm32h7` from one of the
# PRD §11 M10 examples (01-elementwise-add / 05-stencil /
# 09-producer-consumer, naive). This script is EXAMPLE-AGNOSTIC: it injects
# whatever $input fixture it is handed into axiSram, loads whatever $bin ELF
# it is handed, and captures USART1 verbatim — the firmware loads its REAL
# input from the injected region, computes the example's kernels, and
# streams the RAW output bytes over USART1; the `renode-embedded` just
# recipe `cmp`s the captured bytes BYTE-EXACT against the example's
# reference.bin (PRD §10.3 point 3). The per-example differences (which
# algo/sched to generate, which reference.bin to diff) live in the recipe,
# not here.
#
# Caller injects three path variables before `include`-ing this script:
#   $bin      = @<path to the cross-compiled GENERATED firmware ELF>
#   $uartFile = @<path the USART1 file backend writes to>
#   $input    = @<path to the chosen example's input.bin fixture>

mach create "h7"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/cpus/stm32h743.repl

# Deterministic file capture of USART1 (the STM32F7_USART model at
# 0x40011000). Second arg = overwrite-existing.
usart1 CreateFileBackend $uartFile true

# TASK-0048.02 real input path: inject the input fixture into axiSram @
# 0x24000000 BEFORE loading the firmware (and well before RunFor). axiSram
# is mapped in the platform (512K) but NOT in the firmware's memory.x
# linker map, so the stack/.bss never collide with the injected bytes. The
# firmware's Usart1Shim::alloc_in_region reads from this fixed address.
sysbus LoadBinary $input 0x24000000

sysbus LoadELF $bin

# Bounded virtual-time run — the firmware loads its input, computes, and
# streams its output bytes (1024 for ex1/ex5, 64 for ex9) in microseconds,
# then spins. No wall-clock dependence, fully determinate.
emulation RunFor "0.05"
quit
